  "prefLabel": "Tra 503.01 Adoption of Federal Relocation Requirements",
  "priorExpiration": "2015-02-17",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Tra 503.01 Adoption of Federal Relocation Requirements. Pursuant to RSA 124-A:13, all transportation relocation assistance services and benefits offered by the department shall comply with:\n\n(a) The Uniform Relocation Assistance and Real Property Acquisition Policies Act of 1970, as amended, codified as 42 USC sections 4601 through 4655, as amended;\n\n(b) The accompanying regulations to the act referred to in (a) above, found at 49 CFR Part 24, with the exception that the limit of $10,000 contained in 49 CFR 24.304 is modified to $100,000 pursuant to RSA 124-A:3, I(d); and\n\n(c) RSA 498-A.\n\nSource. #4130, eff 9-10-86, EXPIRED: 9-10-92\n\nNew. #6132, eff 11-28-95, EXPIRED: 11-28-03\n\nNew. #8820, eff 2-17-07, EXPIRED: 2-17-15\n\nNew. #11037, eff 2-22-16",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/tra500.html"
